WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.101 --> 00:00:02.201
[music playing]

00:00:02.268 --> 00:00:03.669
WIL WILLIS: David,
Jordan, congratulations.

00:00:03.736 --> 00:00:05.905
You've made it into the third
round of this competition.

00:00:05.972 --> 00:00:07.073
Good job.

00:00:07.139 --> 00:00:08.407
If you thought the last
six hours was tough,

00:00:08.474 --> 00:00:10.543
it's nothing compared
to the next five days

00:00:10.610 --> 00:00:12.478
because we're sending you
back to your home forges

00:00:12.511 --> 00:00:15.181
to recreate an iconic
weapon from history.

00:00:15.248 --> 00:00:16.416
And that weapon is--

00:00:19.419 --> 00:00:21.554
the Talwar pommel.

00:00:21.588 --> 00:00:22.755
[music playing]

00:00:22.788 --> 00:00:24.657
JORDAN: I could comfortably make
a blade like this in a week.

00:00:24.724 --> 00:00:28.094 line:0%
And I can uncomfortably
make one in five days.

00:00:28.161 --> 00:00:29.729
WIL WILLIS: After five
days, you will return

00:00:29.796 --> 00:00:30.997
and present your
finished Talwars

00:00:31.063 --> 00:00:32.498
to our panel of expert judges.

00:00:32.565 --> 00:00:34.267
Only after they've put
them through a series

00:00:34.333 --> 00:00:36.469
of brutal tests will
they declare one of you

00:00:36.536 --> 00:00:39.272
the "Forged in Fire"
champion who also walks away

00:00:39.338 --> 00:00:41.740
with that check for 10 grand.

00:00:41.807 --> 00:00:42.775
Good luck, bladesmiths.

00:00:42.842 --> 00:00:43.943
We'll see you in five days.

00:00:44.010 --> 00:00:47.513 line:7%
[music playing]

00:00:47.580 --> 00:00:48.547 line:7%
DAVID: It's day one.

00:00:48.614 --> 00:00:51.117
We're at my home forge
in Kalkaska, Michigan.

00:00:51.151 --> 00:00:54.887
Hopefully, today I can
get my blade rough forged.

00:00:54.953 --> 00:00:56.455
That-- that's the plan anyway.

00:00:56.489 --> 00:01:00.259
[music playing]

00:01:00.326 --> 00:01:04.030
I've never done a sword of
this magnitude, of difficulty.

00:01:04.096 --> 00:01:07.400
So we'll see how it turns out.

00:01:07.466 --> 00:01:10.536
I just got to make it perfect
because my competitor is

00:01:10.603 --> 00:01:11.471
really good.

00:01:11.538 --> 00:01:14.807
[music playing]

00:01:14.841 --> 00:01:18.010
So day one, I'd like to be
a little further, of course.

00:01:18.077 --> 00:01:20.012
But all in all, it's
been a good day.

00:01:20.079 --> 00:01:22.749 line:7%
[music playing]

00:01:22.782 --> 00:01:24.450 line:7%
JORDAN: It's day two.

00:01:24.517 --> 00:01:26.319
I'm trying to get
this blade a little

00:01:26.385 --> 00:01:28.287
longer to fit the parameters.

00:01:28.353 --> 00:01:29.422
I'm getting a little worried.

00:01:29.455 --> 00:01:31.290
This fuller is
buckled right here.

00:01:31.324 --> 00:01:32.725
When the fuller
starts to buckle,

00:01:32.791 --> 00:01:36.129
it means that the-- the wall
on either side is really thin,

00:01:36.196 --> 00:01:37.430
and it's starting
to move around.

00:01:37.497 --> 00:01:39.999
And there's a danger of
grinding through when

00:01:40.066 --> 00:01:41.300
you go to the grinder.

00:01:41.367 --> 00:01:43.803
So I'm gonna start
this blade over.

00:01:43.870 --> 00:01:48.308
[music playing]

00:01:49.442 --> 00:01:52.345
Back to working on the fuller.

00:01:52.411 --> 00:01:56.782
I'm a little behind
where I hoped I'd be.

00:01:56.815 --> 00:02:00.787
And I'm exhausted.

00:02:00.820 --> 00:02:01.688
Finally.

00:02:01.754 --> 00:02:04.323 line:7%
If you want to call that good.

00:02:04.356 --> 00:02:06.125 line:7%
DAVID: All right, day four.

00:02:06.191 --> 00:02:07.360
The blade is done.

00:02:07.426 --> 00:02:09.194
Now, it's time for the handle.

00:02:09.261 --> 00:02:11.297
I've never made an
entirely metal handle.

00:02:11.364 --> 00:02:13.566
A handle is a tricky
piece of forge work.

00:02:13.633 --> 00:02:15.301
So I'm a little nervous.

00:02:15.367 --> 00:02:17.637
This is as hard as I expected.

00:02:17.704 --> 00:02:21.073
[music playing]

00:02:21.107 --> 00:02:22.708
It's cracking like crazy.

00:02:22.775 --> 00:02:24.610
I'm seeing all these
cracks in my handle.

00:02:24.677 --> 00:02:27.146
And I don't have
any way to fix them.

00:02:27.212 --> 00:02:28.514
I'm starting over.

00:02:28.581 --> 00:02:31.084
Restarting the handle puts
me about five hours behind.

00:02:31.150 --> 00:02:32.585
It's going to be crunch time.

00:02:32.652 --> 00:02:35.254
I'm ready to be done
with this handle.

00:02:35.321 --> 00:02:36.956
I was determined
not to screw it up.

00:02:37.022 --> 00:02:38.658
And here I am,
screwing it up again.

00:02:38.725 --> 00:02:40.827
[music playing]

00:02:41.995 --> 00:02:44.096 line:0%
JORDAN: Day five, I
had this crazy idea

00:02:44.163 --> 00:02:45.531 line:7%
of doing a Damascus handle.

00:02:45.597 --> 00:02:47.767
But the Damascus that
I made was too hard.

00:02:47.800 --> 00:02:53.106
So we're going with plan B,
which is the hollow form pipe.

00:02:53.173 --> 00:02:54.941
I don't know why I didn't
think of this sooner.

00:02:55.008 --> 00:02:57.043
[music playing]

00:02:57.109 --> 00:03:00.880
The advantage of
this was no drilling.

00:03:00.946 --> 00:03:02.615
It's pretty much ready to go.

00:03:02.682 --> 00:03:05.451
And so now, we're actually
going to get the blade polished,

00:03:05.518 --> 00:03:09.288
get the handle welded up,
get it epoxied to the blade.

00:03:09.355 --> 00:03:11.824
I'm feeling relieved.

00:03:11.891 --> 00:03:13.826
And then chop some stuff.

00:03:13.893 --> 00:03:15.527
[music playing]

00:03:15.594 --> 00:03:16.095
There we go.

00:03:16.162 --> 00:03:20.567
[music playing]

00:03:21.233 --> 00:03:22.868
That makes me happy.

00:03:22.935 --> 00:03:23.836
Nice.

00:03:23.902 --> 00:03:24.871
J NEILSON: All right, gentlemen.

00:03:24.904 --> 00:03:26.272
This is the sharpness test.

00:03:26.339 --> 00:03:28.608
Now, the Talwar was a blade
respected throughout India.

00:03:28.674 --> 00:03:30.175
So to test the
sharpness of your blade,

00:03:30.242 --> 00:03:32.045
I'll be cutting
into the sugarcanes.

00:03:32.111 --> 00:03:32.845
David, you're up.

00:03:32.912 --> 00:03:33.612
You ready?

00:03:33.679 --> 00:03:34.313
 Absolutely.

00:03:34.380 --> 00:03:35.114
J NEILSON: All right.

00:03:35.181 --> 00:03:36.248
[music playing]

00:03:36.315 --> 00:03:38.317
DAVID: I-- I know
my weapon is sharp.

00:03:38.383 --> 00:03:40.886
But there's always that
little bit of doubt.

00:03:40.920 --> 00:03:45.458
[music playing]

00:03:55.801 --> 00:03:58.538
J NEILSON: Looks like the
sugarcane speaks for itself.

00:03:58.604 --> 00:04:00.172
There's a lot of weight in this.

00:04:00.205 --> 00:04:01.206
But it's not bad.

00:04:01.273 --> 00:04:03.408
It's balanced very well.

00:04:03.442 --> 00:04:05.511
So the design of
your knuckle bow

00:04:05.577 --> 00:04:07.413
being inside where
this-- this pommel

00:04:07.447 --> 00:04:10.683
is, if my hand slips back there,
I'm kind of whacking into that.

00:04:10.750 --> 00:04:12.184
But it's sharp.

00:04:12.251 --> 00:04:12.985
Nicely done.

00:04:13.052 --> 00:04:13.786
 Thank you.

00:04:13.853 --> 00:04:15.020
 All right, Jordan.

00:04:15.087 --> 00:04:15.854
You ready?

00:04:15.921 --> 00:04:16.656
 I'm ready.

00:04:16.723 --> 00:04:17.790
 OK, let's do this.

00:04:17.824 --> 00:04:22.762
[music playing]

00:04:31.437 --> 00:04:34.874
I just love sabers.

00:04:34.940 --> 00:04:35.975
This is a cutter.

00:04:36.042 --> 00:04:36.775
It's fast.

00:04:36.842 --> 00:04:37.977
It's light.

00:04:38.043 --> 00:04:40.913
But the profile of your handle
could be a little bit larger

00:04:40.980 --> 00:04:41.914
for my hand.

00:04:41.981 --> 00:04:43.683
But all in all, the cuts
speak for themselves.

00:04:43.750 --> 00:04:46.919
It just passed through with
no resistance whatsoever.

00:04:46.986 --> 00:04:48.054
Nicely done.

00:04:48.121 --> 00:04:50.923
DAVID: Our blades, they're
performing almost identical.

00:04:50.990 --> 00:04:52.158
This is going to be tight.

00:04:52.224 --> 00:04:54.493
 The Talwar, a
battle-tested weapon.

00:04:54.560 --> 00:04:57.497
But what kind of lethal
damage does this weapon do?

00:04:57.563 --> 00:04:59.465
To find that out, I
will take your weapon

00:04:59.498 --> 00:05:02.735
and deliver killing blows
on this ballistics dummy.

00:05:02.802 --> 00:05:03.602
David, you're up first.

00:05:03.669 --> 00:05:04.169
You ready?

00:05:04.236 --> 00:05:05.004
 Oh, yeah.

00:05:05.071 --> 00:05:06.238
 Let's do this.

00:05:06.271 --> 00:05:08.908
DAVID: Doug and the
ballistics dummy, this

00:05:08.975 --> 00:05:10.977
is the test that
I wanted to see.

00:05:11.043 --> 00:05:12.711
I'm just, like, super excited.

00:05:12.745 --> 00:05:17.717
[music playing]

00:05:29.261 --> 00:05:30.662
DOUG MARCAIDA: Your
edge of your blade

00:05:30.696 --> 00:05:32.832
is sharp enough to
cut and lacerate

00:05:32.898 --> 00:05:36.769
the whole torso here, cutting
deep and cutting into bone.

00:05:36.836 --> 00:05:39.939
Same thing with the clavicle
over here and into the ribs.

00:05:40.006 --> 00:05:43.275
Your handle construction is a
little bit on the wider side.

00:05:43.342 --> 00:05:44.677
But it's wieldable.

00:05:44.743 --> 00:05:48.681
Overall, your weapon will kill.

00:05:48.748 --> 00:05:49.881
Good job.

00:05:49.948 --> 00:05:50.883
 Thank you.

00:05:50.916 --> 00:05:51.684
 Jordan, you're next.

00:05:51.751 --> 00:05:52.618
You ready?

00:05:52.685 --> 00:05:53.419
 I'm ready.

00:05:53.485 --> 00:05:54.253
DOUG MARCAIDA: Let's do this.

00:05:54.320 --> 00:05:58.358
[music playing]

00:06:05.898 --> 00:06:06.632
All right, Jordan.

00:06:06.699 --> 00:06:07.900
Let's talk about your blade.

00:06:07.967 --> 00:06:10.302
Your edge geometry here
definitely lends itself

00:06:10.369 --> 00:06:11.804
to be a very good thruster.

00:06:11.871 --> 00:06:14.006
It's sliced in easily.

00:06:14.073 --> 00:06:15.975
Your edge is razor sharp.

00:06:16.042 --> 00:06:19.945
But I'm able to lacerate into
the dummy and break some bones.

00:06:20.012 --> 00:06:22.715
Your handle, it's a little
bit on the skinny side.

00:06:22.782 --> 00:06:27.152
But I'm still able to
index and hold onto it.

00:06:27.219 --> 00:06:29.288
Your weapon will kill.

00:06:29.322 --> 00:06:31.590
JORDAN: After this
round, it feels like 2-2.

00:06:31.657 --> 00:06:33.559
Dave and I still
feel really even.

00:06:33.626 --> 00:06:35.628
 All right, gentlemen,
this is the strength test.

00:06:35.694 --> 00:06:38.897
The Talwar was a battle-tested
weapon known to actually

00:06:38.964 --> 00:06:40.700
take heads in combat.

00:06:40.767 --> 00:06:42.701
To test the strength and
durability of your blades,

00:06:42.768 --> 00:06:46.139
I'll be chopping four times
into these beef rib sides.

00:06:46.172 --> 00:06:49.175
This is not about what your
blade does to the beef,

00:06:49.242 --> 00:06:51.476
but what these ribs
do to your blades.

00:06:51.543 --> 00:06:52.645
All right, David, you're up.

00:06:52.712 --> 00:06:53.579
You ready?

00:06:53.646 --> 00:06:55.214
 Ready as I'll ever be.

00:06:55.248 --> 00:06:57.083
A side of beef is
extremely tough.

00:06:57.150 --> 00:06:59.919
It can potentially break
a blade, or chip a blade,

00:06:59.986 --> 00:07:00.520
or bend a blade.

00:07:00.586 --> 00:07:02.088
So I'm concerned.

00:07:02.155 --> 00:07:05.758
[music playing]

00:07:05.825 --> 00:07:06.526
Wow.

00:07:16.468 --> 00:07:17.903
J NEILSON: OK, David,
I've got a little bit

00:07:17.970 --> 00:07:21.207
of chipping and rolling
right where the impact is.

00:07:21.274 --> 00:07:22.508
It's not deep.

00:07:22.575 --> 00:07:24.209
But it is there.

00:07:24.276 --> 00:07:26.412
All in all, it felt good.

00:07:26.478 --> 00:07:29.114
All right, Jordan, you ready?

00:07:29.181 --> 00:07:31.050
 I guess so.

00:07:31.117 --> 00:07:32.285
I'm pretty nervous.

00:07:32.351 --> 00:07:33.886
You know, getting through the
bone is going to be tricky.

00:07:33.952 --> 00:07:36.322 line:0%
And all I can think
is, please don't chip.

00:07:36.388 --> 00:07:37.523 line:7%
Please don't chip.

00:07:37.557 --> 00:07:42.061
[music playing]

00:07:49.235 --> 00:07:50.736
 Took a little
shrapnel off that one.

00:07:52.905 --> 00:07:57.175
I can run my fingernail
along that edge

00:07:57.242 --> 00:07:58.544
and not feel anything.

00:07:58.577 --> 00:08:01.279
No bumps, no chips,
still straight.

00:08:01.313 --> 00:08:03.348
Everything's still tight.

00:08:03.415 --> 00:08:04.249
Good job.

00:08:04.316 --> 00:08:05.317
 Thank you.

00:08:05.384 --> 00:08:07.520
I'm breathing a
huge sigh of relief.

00:08:07.587 --> 00:08:09.889
But I know that also my
handle is a little small.

00:08:09.956 --> 00:08:12.391
And people have been sent
home for handles before.

00:08:12.458 --> 00:08:16.462
[music playing]

00:08:16.529 --> 00:08:18.164
WIL WILLIS: David,
Jordan, both of you

00:08:18.197 --> 00:08:19.432
have made excellent blades.

00:08:19.498 --> 00:08:20.966
And you've been
fantastic competitors.

00:08:21.000 --> 00:08:22.568
But in this arena
of competition,

00:08:22.602 --> 00:08:24.903
there can only be one
"Forged in Fire" champion.

00:08:24.970 --> 00:08:27.673
Before I announce who
that is, the judges have

00:08:27.739 --> 00:08:30.109
some feedback for both of you.

00:08:30.142 --> 00:08:31.576
J NEILSON: Dave, you
brought us a weapon

00:08:31.643 --> 00:08:33.312
that was a pleasure to use.

00:08:33.379 --> 00:08:34.580
It's a heavy weapon.

00:08:34.647 --> 00:08:37.149 line:0%
But you balanced
it out beautifully.

00:08:37.216 --> 00:08:38.116
Nice job.

00:08:38.183 --> 00:08:39.118
 Thank you.

00:08:39.184 --> 00:08:40.253
WIL WILLIS: Doug?

00:08:40.319 --> 00:08:42.455 line:0%
 Jordan, the artistry
of your handle

00:08:42.521 --> 00:08:44.457 line:0%
is matched by the
beauty, strength,

00:08:44.490 --> 00:08:46.592 line:7%
and sharpness of your blade.

00:08:46.626 --> 00:08:47.626 line:7%
Well done, sir.

00:08:47.693 --> 00:08:49.127
WIL WILLIS: Gentlemen,
when weapons

00:08:49.161 --> 00:08:51.897
of this caliber come into
this arena, these decisions

00:08:51.964 --> 00:08:53.466
are never easy.

00:08:53.499 --> 00:09:00.039
The "Forged in Fire"
champion is Jordan.

00:09:00.106 --> 00:09:01.373
Congratulations.

00:09:01.440 --> 00:09:03.009
You are the "Forged
in Fire" champion.

00:09:03.075 --> 00:09:04.877
 Congratulations.

00:09:04.944 --> 00:09:07.379
J NEILSON: David, you
created a beautiful weapon.

00:09:07.445 --> 00:09:08.881
And it was a pleasure to use it.

00:09:08.948 --> 00:09:12.551
And this decision came down to
the finest details, basically

00:09:12.618 --> 00:09:15.621
the positioning of that
knuckle bow on the handle

00:09:15.687 --> 00:09:17.757
and those chips that
turned up in your blade

00:09:17.790 --> 00:09:18.990
in the strength test.

00:09:19.024 --> 00:09:20.759
For those two reasons,
we're letting you go.

00:09:20.793 --> 00:09:22.628
WIL WILLIS: David, please
surrender your weapon.

00:09:22.662 --> 00:09:25.397
[music playing]

00:09:25.463 --> 00:09:28.100
DAVID: Absolutely no regrets.

00:09:28.167 --> 00:09:29.634
I would have liked
to have done better.

00:09:29.668 --> 00:09:31.637
But I agree with the
judge's decision.

00:09:31.704 --> 00:09:32.871
I came here to
prove that I could

00:09:32.938 --> 00:09:35.273
hang with some of
the best bladesmiths

00:09:35.340 --> 00:09:36.475
in the United States.

00:09:36.542 --> 00:09:40.079
And I think I proved
that I can do that.

00:09:40.146 --> 00:09:41.046
 Jordan, congratulations.

00:09:41.080 --> 00:09:42.548
You are the "Forged
in Fire" champion

00:09:42.615 --> 00:09:45.117
and will be receiving
that check for $10,000.

00:09:45.151 --> 00:09:46.118
How do you feel right now?

00:09:46.185 --> 00:09:47.686
 I feel great.

00:09:47.752 --> 00:09:50.022
And I feel pretty accomplished.

00:09:50.088 --> 00:09:51.056
 Well, you should.

00:09:51.123 --> 00:09:53.159
JORDAN: What a great way
to jump start my career,

00:09:53.225 --> 00:09:55.527
you know, making really
high quality blades.

00:09:55.560 --> 00:09:56.829
 Well done.

00:09:56.895 --> 00:09:59.164
JORDAN: This is what I really
wanted for a long time.

00:09:59.231 --> 00:10:00.232
That's why I came here.

00:10:00.299 --> 00:10:01.233
Thank you.

00:10:01.299 --> 00:10:02.134
I'm "Forged in Fire" champion.

00:10:02.168 --> 00:10:05.871
[music playing]

